{
    "background_story": "Azael was a brilliant and eccentric chemist who spent most of his life studying the works of Svante Arrhenius, the Swedish Nobel laureate. Fascinated by Arrhenius' theory of acid-base reactions, Azael dedicated himself to expanding on the concept. He spent years in his laboratory, conducting experiments and gathering data, often neglecting his own well-being in the process. Azael's obsession with Arrhenius' work led him to make a groundbreaking discovery, one that challenged the conventional understanding of chemical reactions. His findings, though initially met with skepticism, eventually earned him recognition within the scientific community. Azael's work built upon the foundation laid by Arrhenius, and his contributions to the field of chemistry were hailed as a testament to the power of perseverance and intellectual curiosity.",
